I find the following notes: the OpenStack community does not publish any official pre-built containers to public registries for the 2026.1 series.Whether using quay.io/openstack.kolla or docker.io/kolla/, pulling will explicitly fail with a repository does not exist or pull access denied error. This happens because upstream OpenStack now treats the kolla-build process strictly as an engine; operators are required to compile their own image sets natively for modern releases.To safely pass your local mirror/pull engine loops without throwing failures, you must drop the unavailable upstream registries entirely and configure your script to look directly at your local image generation workspace.The Real Fix: Swap the Array to Your Local Registry NamingSince you are pulling images into an environment (likely an air-gapped site or local cluster mirror), you must build these 26 containers first on an internet-connected staging machine, push them to your local storage engine, and adjust your array strings to pull from there.Here is how your custom array block should be written, pointing to your local infrastructure registry ip/port (e.g., 127.0.0.1:4000 or your company's inner mirror hostname):bash# ── Local Registry Var (Change to your actual deployment IP/Domain) ──
LOCAL_REGISTRY="127.0.0.1:4000/kolla"

IMAGES=(
  # ... (Keep all your verified Kubernetes / Core Infra elements here unchanged) ...

  # ── OpenStack Kolla Local Images (Built & Verified Locally) ───────────
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-heat-api:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-heat-engine:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-keystone:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-keystone-fernet:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-glance-api:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-placement-api:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-nova-api:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-nova-compute:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-nova-conductor:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-nova-scheduler:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-nova-novncproxy:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-nova-libvirt:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-neutron-server:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-neutron-ovn-metadata-agent:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-ovn-controller:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-ovn-northd:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-ovn-nb-db-server:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-ovn-sb-db-server:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-horizon:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-openvswitch-db-server:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-openvswitch-vswitchd:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-ovn-bgp-agent:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-skyline-apiserver:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-skyline-console:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-cloudkitty-api:2026.1.0"
  "${LOCAL_REGISTRY}/ubuntu-noble-cloudkitty-processor:2026.1.0"

  # ── FOSSBilling + Mirror Prereqs ───────────────────────────────────────
  "docker.io/fossbilling/fossbilling:latest"
  "docker.io/library/mariadb:11"
  "docker.io/library/nginx:1.27-alpine"
  "docker.io/library/registry:2"
)
Use code with caution.Quick Verification Checklist to Generate These ImagesTo populate the registry path above without running into empty target errors:Generate images via pip source build:bashpip install kolla==22.1.0  # Matches 2026.1 cycle dev boundaries
Use code with caution.Compile the targets execution command:bashkolla-build \
  --base ubuntu \
  --base-tag noble \
  --openstack-release 2026.1 \
  --registry 127.0.0.1:4000 \
  --namespace kolla \
  --push \
  heat-api heat-engine keystone glance-api placement-api nova-api nova-compute nova-conductor nova-scheduler nova-novncproxy nova-libvirt neutron-server neutron-ovn-metadata-agent ovn-controller ovn-northd ovn-nb-db-server ovn-sb-db-server horizon openvswitch-db-server openvswitch-vswitchd ovn-bgp-agent skyline-apiserver skyline-console cloudkitty-api cloudkitty-processor

